nds on a massless complex modulus? The selected mixed-modulus channel tests the first mass derivatives and an independent mixed second derivative.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:434a008fcd83da7bf31b345fb2a339cb0587c409bdee7ab87dbcb1773e7e6120","title":"Can spin-zero and spin-one double-trace anomalous dimensions constrain quartic interactions? The source connects this unresolved AdS question with the first two coefficients of a forward-scattering expansion in Minkowski space.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0053"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43e366899f7da3ff10b67ca5fe08b66383a741cb28085d0cc4d19048977a4f2c","title":"How can charge, tension and a Weak Gravity Conjecture be defined for four-dimensional strings and membranes when their backreaction prevents an asymptotically free-state description?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4388ba5c525b417e4a3e81463cabf723b16fda2447df04105d5d37c95b9f7fad","title":"Can many distinct, nearly degenerate fermionic species constitute ultralight dark matter while evading the single-species Tremaine-Gunn bound, and what gravitational production, cosmological, and black-hole constraints limit their number?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0056"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:4311a52b98bb1e25a2ad37027b3d24f707871f2dc59eb42f5d9f1dceff11aa8b","title":"The setting addresses stabilization of compact dimensions by a gas of extended strings in a classical cosmological background.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43fda4d7377e671d1e5ff9ae90acaea7d3551db4c167bec4cf264da092be6f12","title":"How do spacetime spin structures enter the worldsheet description of Type II compactifications on compact Ricci-flat spin 3-manifolds, and what winding tachyons and one-loop vacuum energies diagnose their non-supersymmetric instabilities? The motivation is the conjectured relation between physical stability and special holonomy.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43be8448f4682498cc452befddd47cf57622a14b9ca6e1676e7f8a887d285ace","title":"Can Lorentzian WKB methods describe scalar vacuum transitions with gravity, recover Euclidean transition exponents, and permit closed post-transition universes without the CDL analytic continuations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0059"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43d07874916cb7cae9b86589e4b28d78b9f17a43b2d0aedc350159a38c1a292f","title":"Can eternal de Sitter be a vacuum of interacting S-matrix quantum gravity, and does corpuscular quantum breaking explain the obstruction and yield observable inflationary imprints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43e363fb9814337b83f0e03a93aba748c0f6d3edcefbc7c8dd35b229fbb91478","title":"Which positivity constraints on low-energy scalar scattering survive broken Lorentz boosts, and what do they imply for superfluids, inflationary non-Gaussianity, and the scale where additional physics or nonperturbative effects become necessary?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0062"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:43122f8a1623bc10111335055308ba9510767a4dc01cdb3615280b63afd69ed4","title":"Which protected objects can constrain the gap of six-dimensional F-theory vacua? Wrapped D3 strings are accessible through the tensor sector even though KK modes, generic string excitations, and charged-particle masses are not reliably computable.","conne